			<div class="content" id="post-content-1404086">
									

<blockquote>
<p>So someone who comes under the effect of the SCP will struggle to retain eye contact, and will try to re-establish eye contact if it's broken?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That was my intent. L. was only able to because he was doggedly persistent about resisting it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Can someone actually survive for two days near the summit in a sleeping bag?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>L. is based on the real-life Lincoln Hall, who did indeed survive over 24 hours near the summit in a sleeping bag. Two days might be pushing the limits of possibility, but not quite impossible.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;an effort of unprecedented scale&quot; doesn't seem to me like the sort of thing that would go into a dry report by the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I borrowed that line directly from the Wikipedia article on Hall. Cheerfully withdrawn.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This makes it sound like he became afraid of mountains because he remembered the encounter. Did the Foundation not dose him with amnesiacs?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>He would indeed have been dosed, but like the real Hall retired because of the physical trauma he suffered.</p>

							</div>

								
					
